description:
**Files:** `vibrantix-client-panel/src/components/evidence-management/control-mapping/ControlMappingTable.jsx:83-97`; also duplicated in `control-mapping/tabs/ApprovedMappingsTable.jsx:25-33`
**Root Cause:** The version/provider badge renderer's if/else-if ladder still only matches `aws_`/`_aws`, `azure`, `gcp`, and `k8s`/`kubernetes` — confirmed no `iso27001`/`ISO`/`27001` branch exists in either file. A framework named `iso27001_2022` falls through with no provider badge.
**Re-verified 2026-08-27:** STILL OPEN, and the same unhandled logic is now duplicated in a second file (`ApprovedMappingsTable.jsx`), doubling the maintenance burden of the fix.
**Claude Fix Prompt:**
```
Files: ControlMappingTable.jsx AND ApprovedMappingsTable.jsx (fix both — the logic is duplicated)

In the badge renderer function, add before the cloud-provider checks:
  if (rawName.toLowerCase().includes('iso27001') || rawName.toLowerCase().includes('27001')) {
    const year = rawName.match(/\d{4}/)?.[0];
    provider = year >= 2022 ? 'ISO 27001:2022' : 'ISO 27001:2013 (superseded)';
  }
Consider extracting the shared badge logic into one utility function imported by both files instead of maintaining two copies.
```
